who are the top 10 greatest warriors in  a song of ice and fire which characters  are best at fighting in their prime  years with their usual weapons and armor  this ranking is based on the books in  the time period of the main series and  robert's rebellion no dragons or warging  or magic allowed giants and white  walkers don't count  the number 10 best warrior is victarion  greyjoy the iron captain  victarion wasn't in the tv show but he's  an uncle of theon and asher and  victarion is renowned among the ironborn  as a fearsome warrior he's a big man  strong as a bull and about as smart as a  bull but that just makes him braver  victarion wears heavy plate armor even  in sea battles which is dangerous  because he could drown if he falls  overboard but victarion is afraid of  nothing he lives to fight he was put on  this earth to deal death with his axe in  book four victarion single-handedly  slaughters a bunch of men in battle then  he kills a knight called talbot sarri  sarri is fast but victarion's fast too  catching ceres sword in his armored hand  victarion's hand gets wounded and  infected so a red priest called macquaro  heals victarion's hand with magic and  now vick's arm is burned black and  smoking and is stronger than ever  victarion lifts a man in the air and  kills him with just this bare hand  so with his new super strong barbecue  fist victarion may be even more  dangerous than before  but we never see victarion fight any  really skilled opponents talbot sarri is  not a particularly renowned knight and  victarion's bravery does border on  stupidity so while victarion is powerful  there are better fighters  number nine is loris tyrell the knight  of flowers loris is just 16 years old in  book one but he's already famous as a  great knight he's graceful and quick and  very skilled at fighting author george  martin said that lloris is one of the  best swordsmen in westeros and he's  extremely good at jousting in  tournaments but oberyn martell questions  whether loris is any good in actual  battle so what fights has loris won we  see loris lose a fight with brienne in a  melee loris kills two knights who were  on his side out of mad grief lloris  apparently fought magnificently at the  battle of the blackwater but not as  magnificently as his brother garland in  book five loris leads a savage assault  on dragonstone and kills a bunch of men  but lloris gets badly wounded and doused  in boiling oil and is expected to die  so loris is a talented fighter but he  doesn't have many impressive fates of  battle and his arrogant recklessness is  a weakness that may have just got him  killed jaime thinks lloris has the  potential to be great but so far that  potential is unfulfilled  number eight is brienne the maid of  tarth brienne is freakishly big and  strong she's well over six feet tall  bigger and stronger than jaime she's a  skilled fighter and moves shockingly  fast in battle and she's even more  dangerous with the valyrian steel sword  oathkeeper  in book 2 brienne wins a melee at  renly's camp she's the last standing of  116 nights and she personally defeats  loris tyrell one of the best warriors  alive though loris claims that she won  with a trick by tackling him brienne  often uses her size and strength to  overwhelm opponents her fighting style  is similar to that of her ancestor  duncan the tall  after renly dies brienne fights off a  bunch of his men with speed and skill  and in book three brienne fights jaime  lannister one of the best swordsmen in  westeros it's a long hard fight but try  as he might jaime can't kill her and  eventually brienne beats the kingslayer  though she realizes that jaime is  weakened from months of imprisonment and  his hands are chained together so  brienne thinks that jaime would have won  if he was at his full strength in book  four brienne fights some of the brave  companions or bloody mamas a mercenary  group of absolute frothing psychos  brienne kills three of them in a 1v3  fight with a little help from pod and in  the next fight she kills raj the mad dog  of saltpans but then biter tackles her  and eats some of brienne's face before  she's saved by gendry so brienne is  often underestimated for being a woman  but with her great strength skill and  sheer tenacity brienne wins a lot of  fights and defeats some of the greatest  knights in westeros  number seven is garland tyrell the  gallant garland wasn't in the tv show  but in the books he's an older brother  of loris garland isn't as famous as  loris but he is bigger and stronger and  laura says that garland is a better  swordsman than him author george martin  said the same thing we see that garland  often trains by fighting three or four  men at once so that he's better prepared  for real battle  garland fights magnificently at the  battle of the blackwater he kills guyard  morrigan in single combat and a dozen  other great knights when margaery faces  a trial by combat it's garland she wants  as her champion  so we haven't seen much of garland but  he's clearly an exceptional warrior  number six is gregor clegane the  mountain that rides gregor is  monstrously huge almost eight feet tall  and weighing 400 pounds or 200 kilos all  of it muscle gregor is inhumanly strong  he often cuts men in half with a single  blow gregor wields a two-handed  greatsword in one hand so he's got a  monstrously long reach he's surprisingly  quick and doesn't seem to feel pain  no other knight in the realm inspires  such terror as the mountain the hound  says that no one could ever withstand  gregor but what are his accomplishments  in combat in book 1 the mountain attacks  loris and the hound and tries to kill  them but he fails the hound stops the  mountain and deflects his massive blows  the mountain fights in some battles in  the war he kills beric dondarrion twice  he kills raymond darry and his horse in  a single blow then in tyrion's trial by  combat gregor fights oberyn martell and  oberyn uses his speed and skill and  poison to mortally wound gregor impaling  him with a spear though gregor still  kills oberyn in the end then the mad  scientist qyburn transforms the mountain  into a mysterious undead warrior called  robert strong this silent knight may be  even more dangerous than the mountain  was but we haven't seen him in action  yet in the books  so the mountain is extremely powerful  but we've never seen him beat a really  top-tier opponent skilled warriors like  oberyn and the hound can stop him so  number five is the hound sandor clegane  the hound is a big man tall muscled like  a bull and he's quick fighting with a  terrible savagery  sandor is a twisted bitter man whose  greatest joy in life is killing he's  been killing men since he was 12 years  old knights lords women and children  everyone knows the hound is deadly with  a sword and his snarling dog helm is  widely feared even jaime says that the  hound is a dangerous powerful warrior  author george martin said the hound is  one of the greatest swordsmen in  westeros and we've seen this in action  in book one the hound stops the mountain  despite all the mountain's strength and  rage he can't kill his brother  the hound flees the battle of the  blackwater because he's afraid of fire  but in book 3 he overcomes his fear to  kill beric dondarrion killing beric is  basically a clegane family tradition at  this point  the hound kills some men at the twins in  a 3v1 fight then with the help of arya  he kills some of gregor's men even  though he's blind drunk the hound's  wounds get infected and he's left for  dead but in book four the hound seems to  have survived and found a peaceful life  as a monk maybe he'll return to fight  his zombie brother in the next book  so the hound has a proven record as a  powerful skilled warrior  but the fourth best warrior in westeros  is a young robert baratheon in book one  robert is fat drunk and past his prime  but 20 years ago when he took the throne  robert was the fiercest warrior in the  realm he was six and a half feet tall  towering over his enemies in his armor  and antlered helmet he had a giant  strength wielding a huge iron warhammer  that ned stark could barely lift in his  rebellion against the targaryens robert  won many battles fighting fearlessly on  the front lines at gulltown he was the  first up the walls and killed lord  grafton by his own hand at summerhall  robert won three battles in one day and  killed lord phil in single combat he  lost a battle at ashford but then he won  the battle of the bells and killed six  men including the famous knight miles  mooton  finally robert won the battle of the  trident personally killing prince  rhaegar targaryen who was renowned as a  skilled warrior and so robert won the  war and became king of westeros making  him one of the most successful warriors  ever he won all these battles personally  killing many knights and lords and no  one ever managed to kill him  except eventually for a pig and his wife  and his crippling alcoholism but in his  prime robert was one of the greatest  warriors in westeros  number three is jaime lannister the  kingslayer before he lost his hand  barristan selmy thinks of jaime as one  of the best natural swordsmen he's seen  jaime says that in his prime he was  bigger stronger and quicker than lloris  he's confident that with his skill and  speed he could beat the mountain and the  hound author george martin often names  jaime as one of if not the best fighters  in westeros he said jaime would beat  aragorn in a fight he said jaime would  beat hermione in a fight he said jaime  could beat a cult of cthulhu  jaime won a tournament melee when he was  just 13 years old at 15 he fought the  kingswood brotherhood and held his own  against the notorious smiling night  jaime was knighted by arthur dayne and  became the youngest kingsguard ever in  the main series he kicks ass in several  battles covering himself in glory he  cuts through edmure's army like an axe  through ripe cheese at the whispering  wood he fights through the northern army  and almost kills robb stark he only  stops because his sword gets stuck in a  north man's skull  even after being imprisoned and weakened  for months he still almost beats brienne  brienne thinks that at his full strength  no knight in the seven kingdoms could  have stood against jaime  once jaime loses his hand he's no longer  a great fighter but his battles his  reputation and the words of the author  show that jaime is one of the best  warriors in westeros  number two is a young barristan selmy  barristan the bold is widely recognized  as the greatest knight alive he is a  living legend when he was young  barristan was the finest sword in the  seven kingdoms and he has a long list of  accomplishments in combat barristan rode  in his first tournament at 10 years old  at 16 he performed great feats of  prowess in a tournament and defeated  duncan the tall lord commander of the  kingsguard at 23 he joined the  kingsguard himself and won many more  victories in tournaments and melees he  defeated all challengers at the silver  bridge  barristan defeated simon toyne of the  kingswood brotherhood barristan ended  the war of the nine penny kings by  killing maelys the monstrous in single  combat and barristan ended the defiance  of duskendale king aerys targaryen got  kidnapped and held hostage by house  darkland so in an act of crazy courage  barristan single-handedly rescued the  king he climbed the walls of duskendale  with his bare hands killed a bunch of  gods and knights and escaped with aerys  despite taking an arrow to the chest  in the battle of the trident barristan  fought for the targaryens but he was so  badass that when robert took over he  decided to keep barristan on the  kingsguard in the time of the main  series barristan is in his 60s and he's  still an exceptional fighter still  winning tournaments still better than  the other kingsguard after he joins  daenerys he kills the titans bastard  with a stick he kills a deadly dothraki  warrior and he leads a cavalry charge in  the siege of moraine barristan has been  winning fights for six decades and is  universally recognised as the greatest  knight alive but there is one warrior  who is better  first some honorable mentions oberyn  martel the red viper has a great  reputation as a warrior and he's very  skilled but the one time we see him  fight he dies  brawn is a deadly warrior who tyrion  compares to jaime thoros of mir beats  the hound in melees three times probably  because thoros uses flaming swords carl  drogo has never lost a fight but we  never see him fight an armored knight  great jon umber is so big and tough that  when his fingers get eaten he laughs  mance raider became king of the  wildlings by killing a bunch of his  rivals andrick the unsmiling is said to  be the greatest fighter in the iron  islands but we don't know anything about  him darkstar is said to be the most  dangerous man in dawn he's also the  edgiest emo in dawn and strong belvos is  such a confident gladiator that he lets  his opponents cut him before he kills  them belvos survives poison eats liver  and onions and takes a literal [ __ ] on  his opponents  the kitten sir pounce has the impressive  combat feat of scaring off bellerion a  notably fearsome tomcat however sir  pounce fails to prevent lady whiskers  from stealing his mouse so sir pouncer's  combat record is mixed at best  so the number one best warrior in  westeros is arthur dayne the sword of  the morning  arthur died 20 years ago but he's  remembered as the deadliest of aerys's  kingsguard deadlier than barristan and  deadlier than jaime jaime says that  arthur could have killed five kingsguard  with his left hand while taking a piss  with his right ned stark said that  arthur was the finest knight he ever saw  arthur wielded the legendary ancient  sword dawn said to be forged from the  heart of a meteor george martin said  that with dorne arthur would beat  barristan in a fight arthur killed the  smiling knight who was like the mountain  of his time  arthur apparently died fighting ned  stark and howland reed in the show it's  revealed that howland stabbed arthur in  the back but in the books this whole  situation is still a mystery there's so  much we don't know about arthur his only  fights mentioned in the books are with  ned stark and the smiling knight so we  only know he's the best warrior ever  because the characters and the authors  say so many characters think of arthur  with nostalgia rose tinted glasses for a  bygone time so was arthur really that  great or is he just the idealized symbol  of a noble knight how can we ever know  if he would have beaten the hound or  brienne in a fight george martin has  said that the whole idea of ranking the  best fighters is kind of dumb there is  no objective answer who would win in a  fight depends on the situation on the  day on random chance it depends on the  relationships and the emotions of the  people involved a song of ice and fire  isn't about the sword fights it's about  the story and the characters and themes  but we won't let that stop us comment  below your top 10 best fighters or top  20 how would you rank oberyn and the  great john and bellewas we have almost  finished two big videos about dune that  will come out soon and the game of  thrones prequel tv show house of the  dragon will start in august we'll make  videos about that too so subscribe to  alt shift x turn on the bell follow the  podcast and thank you to the supporters  on patreon including trish ledoux  baumbart dewees joseph barkermeyer white  fifty ever pat rion stephen hancock 81  carol moraz leia blaze delton imperial  and hierarchical lobster cheers
 

